  "summary": "KREMLIN is a Brazilian banking malware toolkit (REF9334) that chains obfuscated JavaScript loaders, Node.js execution, RunPE/manual mapping or SentinelOne DLL sideloading, and a Chrome/Edge extension installed by regenerating Chromium Secure Preferences HMACs and App-Bound encrypted hashes. The extension steals credentials, cookies, session storage, history, page source and keystrokes and exfiltrates RC4-encrypted ZIP archives over HTTP and WebSocket C2 whose endpoints are resolved through Ethereum smart contracts.",
